ame team.claude configures is legal; one nothing configures refuses by name.\n\n### Command surface\nNames only (197 commands). Flags and usage: before the FIRST use of a verb in a session, read `bee <verb> --help` — never guess flags; one read per verb is enough, never re-read (everything at once: `bee --help --all`); nearly every command also takes a `json` flag (179 of 197).\nbacklog: add, badges, counts, findings, pbi add, pbi amend, pbi list, pbi status, propose, rank, render\nblind: check\ncapture: add, count, flush, list\ncells: add, archive, backfill-roles, block, cap, claim, claim-next, dissent, dissent-verdict, drop, escalate, finish, judge, judge-record, list, ready, reopen, reset-budget, schedule, show, unarchive, unclaim, update\nclose\nconfig: get, set, unset, validate\ndecisions: active, archive, log, reattribute, redact, render, search, supersede, tag\ndev: install-support, plugin-distribution, regen, release-manifest, render-hook-manifests, render-prompt, render-skill-trees, statusline\ndiscovery: list, stub\ndispatch: prepare, wave\ndoctor\ndoctor: attest\nfeedback: collect, count, digest, rank\nfinish\ngate\nherding: agent-start, cancel, classify-lane, command-template, control-loop, disable, enable, herdr-pane-id, herdr-result, interlock, interrupt, occupancy, pane, pane-id, record-worker, result, run, status, wave\nintent: advance, clear, set, show\nknowledge: bootstrap, check, context, index, list, new, promote, report, search, show\nmailbox: mark, reflect\nmodels: show\nonboard\norient\nperf: log, render, report, section, start, stop, sync\nrecovery: scan, window\nreservations: list, release, reserve, sweep\nreviews: candidate add, candidates, create, list, record, show, status\nroute\nrs-info\nshape\nstaging: add, rebuild, status\nstate: advisor-ref record, advisor-ref show, compact-capsule, compact-check, compact-log, compounding-run, gate, handoff adopt, handoff show, handoff write, lanes, plan-conflicts derive, plan-conflicts verdict, plan-rev bump, rebuild-projections, route, scribing-run, session bind, session list, session release, session unbind, set, start-feature, waiting-on clear, waiting-on set, worker add, worker clear, worker prune, worker remove, worker update, workflows close, workflows list\nstatus\nsupervisor: away, back, consent-sweep, list, mark-delivered, metrics, pending, presence, record, report\nteam: show\ntest\ntimings: report\ntmp: sweep\ntriggers: add, list, resolve\nversion\nwork: set, show\nworktree: enter, list, merge, new, prune, register, unregister\n\n### Project map\n- System overview: docs/specs/system-overview.md\n- Reading map: docs/specs/reading-map.md\n- Specced areas: 0 (docs/specs/ — read the spec before the code)\n\n### Critical patterns (digest)\n# Critical Patterns\nMandatory pre-planning / pre-execution context for this repository.\nbee-capturing appends hard-won patterns here; keep it short and current.\n(none captured yet)\n\nEverything above is already read — do not re-fetch it. Run `.bee/bin/bee status --json` yourself when you ROUTE WORK (claim, plan, change phase) or need detail this block does not carry. Never hand bee commands to the user. Route via bee-hive.","stderr":""}
