389:   389	| Spawn | **Native cell refusal on Codex 0.154.0**: native `spawn_agent` delivers opaque messages to hooks, hiding the role marker; `bee dispatch prepare` classifies the client as `native_hook_input_opaque` and refuses native cell dispatch, while `bee hook model-guard` denies unmarked native spawns as transport `codex-spawn-unmarked` (exit 2). Both direct callers to configured herding or CLI routes. For supported capability-probed environments, the callable schema is `spawn_agent({task_name: "<stable-name>", message: "<WORKER_PROMPT>", fork_turns: "none", model?: "<model>", reasoning_effort?: "<effort>"})`: `task_name` and `message` are required; `fork_turns` is a STRING ("none", "all", or positive integer string, e.g. "1", not integer); `model` and `reasoning_effort` are optional; no `agent_type` or `sandbox` field exists. For non-cell read-only jobs (gather, reviewer, advisor), configured herding and CLI routes stay explicit; model-shaped or prompt-budget non-cell roles (including Model, Native and null/budget resolutions) route through an explicit read-only CLI sandbox (`codex exec --sandbox read-only --ephemeral -`) because native spawn provides no filesystem sandbox boundary. Explicit unknown `--role` is refused, never granted fallback. |
390:   390	| Model | `config.team.codex[<role>]` if set; Codex 0.154.0 attaches configured model and reasoning_effort for supported dispatches. Full-history forks cannot carry overrides; escalated cells preserve the parent model without overrides. Unverifiable native dispatches with opaque hook messages are refused. |
391-   391	| Result collection | Status tokens arrive in the parent thread; use `wait_agent(..., timeout_ms=60000)` only when a specific result is needed |
392-   392	| Follow-up / rescue | `followup_task({target: "<agent id or task name>", message: "..."})` to continue the same agent; a fresh `spawn_agent` only for a genuinely new task — no routine `send_input(...)` mid-flight |
393-   393	| Harness assist | None — the tend loop in this skill is the nudge |
394:   394	| Isolation guarantee | `fork_turns: "none"`; never fork the parent history for routine cells |
395:   395	| Subagent type | No per-agent subagent type or native sandbox field — read-only roles enforce filesystem boundaries via the CLI read-only sandbox (`codex exec --sandbox read-only --ephemeral -`); write roles enforce via write-guard hooks or herding/CLI |
